        "call_451143f696d34ed4a6204e75957de47e"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No APT transaction, PowerShell script, GitHub Actions job or wheel build was executed; package availability and successful dependency resolution remain unverified.",
    "The external CUDA action and linked NVIDIA forum explanation were not inspected.",
    "The Python check counted matrix declarations; it did not execute workflow conditions or provisioning."
  ],
  "links": [
    "8a230d7856b3eca45f92a7ec5c843535acdd4021"
  ],
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "build-release",
      "title": "Extend the CUDA package workaround to libnvidia-cfg1",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "After installing and holding nvidia-persistenced, the step now requests libnvidia-cfg1=575.57.08-0ubuntu1 using apt-get install -y --allow-downgrades, then requests apt-mark hold libnvidia-cfg1. The numeric string selects a package release, not a CUDA toolkit version. No APT preference file is added.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": [
            "call_6b519379ebe24537b05faa5976df9d75"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The new commands reuse the existing step's non-Windows/nonempty-CUDA guard and inherited pwsh shell. They follow APT repository setup and index refresh, and precede Jimver/cuda-toolkit@v0.2.25 with matrix.cuda, network installation and --toolkit. The task changes neither that action nor its inputs.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": [
            "call_b2c53f8ef3fb461a94479bf50e1da7c2",
            "call_6b519379ebe24537b05faa5976df9d75"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A bounded Python inspection counted nine parent matrix rows, including four Ubuntu CUDA rows covering Python 3.10–3.13. These rows request CUDA 12.8.1.",
          "basis": "execution",
          "evidence": [
            "call_3c698d51e70444739246b8fd8dfb0f39"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The installation and hold are coupled: installation requests the exact release first, while the following hold seeks to retain the installed package selection. This extends the existing constrained-package strategy rather than changing toolkit selection, trading flexibility for a more specific provisioning environment.",
          "basis": "inference",
          "evidence": [
            "call_6b519379ebe24537b05faa5976df9d75",
            "call_b2c53f8ef3fb461a94479bf50e1da7c2"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [],
  "summary": "Adds exact-version libnvidia-cfg1 installation and hold before Linux CUDA setup, extending the existing nvidia-persistenced workaround without establishing build success."
}
